}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/comments/272933136","html_url":"https://github.com/vimeo/psalm/issues/62#issuecomment-272933136","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/62","id":272933136,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3MjkzMzEzNg==","user":{"login":"svivian","id":207887,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/svivian","html_url":"https://github.com/svivian","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svivian/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svivian/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svivian/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svivian/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svivian/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svivian/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svivian/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svivian/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svivian/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-01-16T18:27:58Z","updated_at":"2017-01-16T18:27:58Z","body":"OK turns out the errors being omitted are due to the command itself, it's not picking up the `psalm.xml` file. Running either of these commands works:\r\n\r\n    psalm --config=psalm.xml\r\n    psalm -c=psalm.xml\r\n\r\nIt's not clear from `psalm --help` that you need the equals. Also, single-dash flags don't usually use equals, it's normally `--flag=value` or `-f value`.\r\n\r\n> Moving entirely to file paths (vs relative paths) seems to have fixed it\r\n\r\nYes, I've updated and the output is consistent now.\r\n\r\n> that file is outside of the config-provided project directories & files, so Psalm doesn't abide by the exclusions dictated in the config\r\n\r\nOK fair enough.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/comments/272933136/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"svivian","id":207887,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzg4Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/svivian","html_url":"https://github.com/svivian","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svivian/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svivian/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svivian/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svivian/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svivian/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svivian/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svivian/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svivian/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svivian/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/comments/272937006","html_url":"https://github.com/vimeo/psalm/issues/62#issuecomment-272937006","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/62","id":272937006,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3MjkzNzAwNg==","user":{"login":"muglug","id":2292638,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTI2Mzg=",